## Goal
Reject passing one enum type where another distinct enum is required (even if int-compatible).

## Source
todo-cover-cases-next.txt — Case 6 (2026-08-11, tm-editor-plus-plus)

## Repro
```angelscript
pmt.RemoveBlockSafe(targetBlock.BlockInfo, coord, targetBlock.Direction);
```

## Compiler (game-side)
```
Components/Cursor/Gizmo.as (544, 39) : ERR : No matching signatures to
'CGameEditorPluginMapMapType::RemoveBlockSafe(CGameCtnBlockInfo@, int3,
 const CGameCtnBlock::ECardinalDirections)'
```
Expected: `CGameEditorPluginMap::ECardinalDirections`, not `CGameCtnBlock::ECardinalDirections`.

## Workaround
`CGameEditorPluginMap::ECardinalDirections(int(targetBlock.Direction))`

## LSP today
0 diagnostics. External method args are not type-checked; `is_convertible` only equates Named types structurally when equal.

## Acceptance
- [ ] External method param types consulted at call sites
- [ ] Distinct Named enum types are not convertible without explicit cast
- [ ] This RemoveBlockSafe callsite diagnoses
- [ ] Valid same-enum calls remain silent
- [ ] Regression test

## Notes
Depends on wiring external signatures into checker (shared with IndexOf / Selectable arity work). Enum distinctness is the type-matching layer on top.